		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43762#p43762"><![CDATA[
It is a tenant of the Bullet API: if you give the <strong class="text-strong">World</strong> an <strong class="text-strong">Action</strong> then the action's <strong class="text-strong">updateAction(world, delta_time)</strong> method will be called once per substep.  All of that happens inside the <strong class="text-strong">stepSimulation()</strong> which is usually called explicitly by your App's code.  If <strong class="text-strong">LibGdx</strong> exposes the <strong class="text-strong">Action</strong> interface then it should be possible to write custom logic that is invoked inside the substep.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11033">drleviathan</a> — Fri Dec 17, 2021 5:41 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
